## Design language derived from KiroCrew

The visual language of this design system — its surface ladder, accent role,
spacing rhythm, control density, radius scale, focus treatment, glass surfaces,
and scrollbar affordances — is substantially translated and modified from
KiroCrew (https://github.com/kirodotdev/KiroCrew):

    Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.
    KiroCrew is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and includes
    software developed at Amazon.com, Inc. (https://www.amazon.com/).

The translation is deliberate and total: KiroCrew's React components and its
bespoke CSS custom properties are re-expressed here as SolidJS components built
on Kobalte and corvu primitives, styled through the shadcn/ui semantic token
vocabulary carried in OKLCH. No KiroCrew source file is reproduced verbatim.

## Consumed libraries

Components are built on the following upstream projects. They are consumed as
dependencies, not copied:

    Kobalte (@kobalte/core)        MIT License
    corvu (@corvu/*)               MIT License
    shadcn/ui                      MIT License
    SolidJS (solid-js)             MIT License
    lucide (lucide-solid)          ISC License
    Tailwind CSS                   MIT License

The component architecture — the folder-per-component layout, the registry
build, and the convention of composing higher-level blocks on top of an
unmodified primitive layer — follows patterns established by the
shadcn-storybook-template (MIT), Kibo UI (MIT), and Dice UI (MIT) projects.

Origin UI / coss (AGPL-3.0-or-later) was consulted for visual ideas only. No
code, class string, or asset from that project is reproduced here, because its
licence is incompatible with this distribution.

## Composer IME input ownership translated from KiroCrew

`packages/ui/src/components/conversation/ime-guard.ts` and its MessageComposer
binding substantially translate the native latch and textarea-scoped lifecycle
from `website/src/hooks/useImeGuard.ts`, pinned at KiroCrew revision
`283e136c0f902e965a535a7c9548c57c7504fed0`.

    Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.
    This product includes software developed at Amazon.com, Inc.
    (https://www.amazon.com/).
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Retained: native isComposing/keyCode229 signals, the 50ms post-composition window,
back-to-back composition fencing, native candidate default actions, and recovery
on focus/blur. Solid owner cleanup replaces React effects/ref ownership; native
propagation replaces React's synthetic-event half. A repeated compositionend
replaces the previous timer so an older expiry cannot release the latest window.
The document-latch/focus-trap branch is not copied: this is one textarea's send
binding, and maintained Kobalte primitives retain overlay focus authority.

Browser integration tests translate relevant cases from
`website/src/test/SideChat.imeEnter.test.tsx` and the lifecycle/window cases in
`website/src/hooks/useImeGuard.documentLatch.test.tsx`; React/Redux/query/API test
providers are replaced by a controlled Solid fixture. No React dependency,
service transport, dictation engine, font, asset or document listener is copied.
This is selected-unit hardening, not a claim that the full KiroCrew composer,
goal flow or Adea runtime-session Chat has been ported or integrated.

## Plain transcript follow translated from KiroCrew

`packages/ui/src/components/conversation/scroll-follow-core.ts`,
`scroll-follow.ts` and ConversationSurface substantially translate the plain
scroller lifecycle in `website/src/app-sdk/useChatScrollFollow.ts` and its pure
`website/src/hooks/virtualizer/FollowController.ts` decisions, pinned at
`283e136c0f902e965a535a7c9548c57c7504fed0`.

    Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.
    This product includes software developed at Amazon.com, Inc.
    (https://www.amazon.com/). Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Retained: separate follow intent and jump visibility, synchronous scroll-up race
fencing, direction-aware re-engagement, self-scroll attribution, DPR tolerance,
content growth/collapse and viewport shrink/growth distinctions, instant pins,
explicit disabled/reset behavior and content/viewport observer cleanup. Solid
ownership replaces React refs/effects. Applications retain identity, durable
scroll restoration and virtualized row measurement/anchor authority.

The jump label follows `website/src/app-sdk/ChatScrollChrome.tsx`'s action-only
contract; pixel distance cannot establish an unread message count. The existing
shared button appearance and configurable 80px visibility default are retained.
Keyboard jumping returns focus to the focusable transcript as its jump control
disappears; this hardens a donor edge case without moving focus during automatic
pins. No donor edge-fade styling, React runtime, virtualizer, asset, font or session
store is copied. Tests translate applicable cases from
`website/src/test/useChatScrollFollow.test.tsx` and `FollowController.test.ts`;
Bun/browser integration and deterministic bounded grids replace React/jsdom,
Vitest and fast-check without adding dependencies. The full Chat product
composition and application adoption remain separate gates.

